{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 756150,
  "courseSlug": "the-complete-guide-to-angular-2",
  "courseTitle": "Angular - The Complete Guide",
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "44115592",
      "title": "Exploring Advanced Content Projection",
      "lectureOrder": 108,
      "videoOrder": 102,
      "sourceHash": "8806eb428dc520c2b4d5354754e638deba941bcdc984f80581d3f480b1c7eaef",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.63,
          "end": 2.76,
          "en": "Now, ng-content has even more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 2.76,
          "end": 4.17,
          "en": "features to offer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.17,
          "end": 7.05,
          "en": "For example, let's say that we don't want to have",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 7.05,
          "end": 10.71,
          "en": "this icon class on a span outside",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 10.71,
          "end": 12.633,
          "en": "of this buttons template here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 13.71,
          "end": 16.8,
          "en": "So we might prefer to have this span",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 16.8,
          "end": 20.73,
          "en": "with this icon class in our button components template.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.73,
          "end": 23.403,
          "en": "And we might wanna wrap that around ng-content.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 25.35,
          "end": 27,
          "en": "Now of course we could do that",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 27,
          "end": 30.69,
          "en": "and still use it in the places where we use the button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 30.69,
          "end": 33.363,
          "en": "to make this icon here selectable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.29,
          "end": 36.33,
          "en": "But if we do that, we of course end up",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 36.33,
          "end": 38.28,
          "en": "with some duplication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 38.28,
          "end": 39.9,
          "en": "If I now inspect the Logout button,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 39.9,
          "end": 43.26,
          "en": "you see that in there we have that icon span",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 43.26,
          "end": 45.09,
          "en": "which includes another span",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 45.09,
          "end": 46.8,
          "en": "with the class icon inside of it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 46.8,
          "end": 50.1,
          "en": "which is an unnecessary duplication.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 50.1,
          "end": 53.31,
          "en": "For situations like this, you can offer another feature",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 53.31,
          "end": 55.17,
          "en": "provided by Angular.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 55.17,
          "end": 57.75,
          "en": "Instead of adding that class here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 57.75,
          "end": 61.41,
          "en": "in the place where you use the button component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 61.41,
          "end": 66.357,
          "en": "you can use the special ngProjectAs attribute,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.23,
          "end": 69.63,
          "en": "which is supported by Angular,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 69.63,
          "end": 71.52,
          "en": "as you can tell by the prefix.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 71.52,
          "end": 75.09,
          "en": "And you can add it on any element that's used anywhere",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.09,
          "end": 78.39,
          "en": "where you're using content projection.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.39,
          "end": 82.26,
          "en": "And it allows you to define a selector",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 82.26,
          "end": 86.4,
          "en": "that can then be matched from inside the component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 86.4,
          "end": 89.673,
          "en": "where you're trying to project this content into.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 91.14,
          "end": 94.08,
          "en": "So here I'm trying to project this icon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.08,
          "end": 95.7,
          "en": "into my button component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.7,
          "end": 97.62,
          "en": "and I can, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 97.62,
          "end": 100.62,
          "en": "project this through the icon selector.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 100.62,
          "end": 103.2,
          "en": "So not the class icon with a dot,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 103.2,
          "end": 105.993,
          "en": "but the element selector, so to say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 107.03999999999999,
          "end": 109.71000000000001,
          "en": "Now I'm not using icon as a HTML element,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 109.71000000000001,
          "end": 114.003,
          "en": "I'm just setting it for the ngProjectAs property here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 115.47,
          "end": 119.13,
          "en": "Now, the effect of that is that in the button component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 119.13,
          "end": 122.1,
          "en": "where I'm selecting content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 126.78,
          "en": "I can now select content that has the element icon,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 126.78,
          "end": 129.15,
          "en": "even though I'm never using that element",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 129.15,
          "end": 133.503,
          "en": "because I'm using this ngProjectAs attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 135.03,
          "end": 139.11,
          "en": "So that simply works together with ng-content,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 139.11,
          "end": 140.97,
          "en": "which therefore allows me to now use",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 140.97,
          "end": 142.803,
          "en": "any selector of my choice.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 144.03,
          "end": 147.39,
          "en": "And I can of course now also go to the new-ticket.component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 147.39,
          "end": 151.89,
          "en": "And there on this span, instead of using this class here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 151.89,
          "end": 156.89,
          "en": "we can also use ngProjectAs and use icon like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 158.82,
          "end": 163.44,
          "en": "And that will then be picked up by the select property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 163.44,
          "end": 166.53,
          "en": "on ng-content in the button component.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 166.53,
          "end": 170.67000000000002,
          "en": "And if we save everything, it'll still work as before,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 170.67000000000002,
          "end": 174.36,
          "en": "but now we don't have that unnecessary wrapping.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 174.36,
          "end": 176.49,
          "en": "We still have a span in a span,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 176.49,
          "end": 179.19,
          "en": "but we only have one span with the class icon.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 179.19,
          "end": 181.89,
          "en": "And before that we had two spans with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 181.89,
          "end": 183.633,
          "en": "which was unnecessary.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 185.04,
          "end": 188.133,
          "en": "And that's therefore another feature you should be aware of.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}
